						blockoverride "tnt_picker_open_enabled" { enabled = "[TntValid('tnt_multi_subject_r_open')]" }
						blockoverride "tnt_picker_open_tooltip" { tooltip = "[TntTip('tnt_multi_subject_r_open')]" }
						blockoverride "tnt_picker_clear_sgui"   { onclick = "[TntExec('tnt_sel_subject_r_clear')]" }
					}
				}
			}
		}

		####################################################################
		### FOOTER
		### Exactly ONE button_primary in this window - it silently binds
		### RETURN and alt+C (GAME\gui\shared\buttons.gui:28-29), so two of
		### them would fight over the same key.
		### enabled / tooltip / onclick all come from the tnt_send_offer
		### scripted gui - the shape of GAME\gui\window_faith.gui:894-905.
		### R-LAYOUT: neither button carries an anchor; `expand = {}` between them
		### is what pushes Propose to the right.
		####################################################################
		hbox = {
			name = "tnt_footer"
			layoutpolicy_horizontal = expanding

			### V3 FIX: an EXPLICIT height. Without it the footer's height was
			### derived from its children, so the vbox above had to guess how much
			### room to leave for it while tnt_table was busy claiming everything it
			### could as an expanding child. A stated height is reserved first and
			### cannot be squeezed out, which is what a bottom bar must do.
			### 58 = the 42 px Propose button plus the 8 px vertical margin twice.
			size = { 100% 58 }

			margin = { 4 8 }
			spacing = 10

			button_standard = {
				name = "tnt_clear_button"
				size = { 190 36 }
				text = "tnt_btn_clear"
				onclick = "[TntExec('tnt_clear_all')]"
			}

			expand = {}

			### THE FOOTER HAS TWO BUTTONS AND NOT THREE.
			###
			### A third one lived here for two iterations: Impose by force, which declared
			### a war whose victory executed the treaty. IT WAS DELETED BY DECISION, not by
			### accident, and the reasoning is recorded in
			### _docs/92-IMPOSE-WAR-REJECTED.md - in short: it duplicated and overshadowed
			### vanilla's own casus belli system, which is the wrong trade for a mod that
			### exists to extend CK3's diplomacy rather than to replace its wars.
			### Do not add it back here.
			button_primary = {
				name = "tnt_propose_button"
				size = { 400 42 }
				text = "tnt_btn_propose"
				enabled = "[TntValid('tnt_send_offer')]"
				tooltip = "[TntTip('tnt_send_offer')]"
				onclick = "[TntExec('tnt_send_offer')]"
			}
		}
	}

	####################################################################
	### PICKER OVERLAY - twelve panels, at most one visible.
	### Panel visibility is a pure variable test: the item index from the
	### frozen index table (R0.8) plus the side. No GetScriptedGui in any
	### visible=. EqualTo_CFixedPoint over a MakeScope value is verbatim
	### vanilla: GAME\gui\activity_window_widgets\debate_success_chance.gui:137.
	### Row shape copied from GAME\gui\activity_window_widgets\
	### funeral_deceased_selection_widget.gui:55-82. Every row is fixed-size.
	###
	### BUILD 2 FILLS THE TWO RESERVED INDICES AND CONVERTS THREE PAIRS.
	###   5      tnt_panel_marriage  - the spouse pair + line editor (item 2.1)
	###   6/7/10 tnt_panel_multi     - available|chosen two-list panels, six
	###                               instances, replacing the single-select
	###                               tnt_picker_panel at those indices (item 2.2)
	###   8      RETIRED (user item 7) - was tnt_picker_panel, the read-only
	###                               dungeon list, one instance per side
	###   11     RETIRED (user item 1) - was tnt_picker_panel, the single-select
	###                               non-aggression third party, one per side
	###   12     tnt_panel_contract  - the nine-row obligation sheet (item 2.5)
	###   13     RETIRED (user item 7) - was tnt_panel_multi_prisoner_p, the
	###                               per-captive selection list; side 1 of this
	###                               index was reserved for a partner-side twin
	###                               and that reservation is released with it
	###
	### ITEM 19 ADDED THREE INDICES AND SIX PANELS, all of them types-only in
	### gui/tnt_panel_people.gui and all instantiated with one line each at the
	### bottom of this block. TWO INDICES AND FOUR PANELS SURVIVE:
	###   16     tnt_panel_hostage_p / _r   - one hostage per side
	###   17     RETIRED V16, USER ITEM 5 - was tnt_panel_ward_p / _r, one child
	###          per side. The type declarations are commented out in
	###          gui/tnt_panel_people.gui section 2 and their two instantiations
	###          at the bottom of this block in the SAME edit: an instantiation
	###          of an undeclared type is a .gui LOAD error. Index dormant.
	###   18     tnt_panel_courtier_p / _r  - courtiers, uncapped since V11,
	###                                       two-list panels like 6 / 7 / 10
	### GRANT INDEPENDENCE, the fourth new term, has NO panel and NO index: a
	### bool pair needs only a checkbox and a gate.
	### V26 ADDED ONE MORE INDEX AND TWO MORE PANELS, the first claim on a free
	### index since 18:
	###   19     tnt_panel_subject_p / _r   - TRANSFER A VASSAL, uncapped,
	###                                       two-list panels of the same shape
	###
	### HOW THE TWO-LIST PANELS WORK, because it is the whole of item 2.2 and it
	### is easy to "simplify" into something broken. A row click MOVES the object
	### between two script variable lists: tnt_pick_<item>_<side>_set does
	### add_to_variable_list on tnt_sel_* plus remove_list_variable from
	### tnt_list_*, and tnt_pick_<item>_<side>_unset does the reverse
	### (30-V2-DESIGN 1 row 2.2, and the move-out idiom is already shipped at
	### MOD\common\scripted_effects\tnt_31_lists.txt). Because the object is only
	### ever in ONE of the two lists, NO membership datafunction is needed
	### anywhere - which is exactly why the design chose two datamodels over one
	### list plus a "is it selected" test that CK3 cannot express. That is also
	### why the available column's rows are `down = no` and the chosen column's
	### are `down = yes`: the column a row is IN is the selection state.
	###
	### The three fill effects are unchanged and still populate tnt_list_title_*,
	### tnt_list_claim_* and tnt_list_artifact_* on window open; only the setters
	### change from set_variable to a list move.
	####################################################################
	tnt_picker_overlay = {
		blockoverride "tnt_picker_panels"
		{
			############################################################
			### 5 - THE MARRIAGE PAIR + LINE EDITOR   (item 2.1)
			###
			### TWO LINES, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE INTEGRATION. `tnt_panel_marriage`
			### carries its own `visible = "[EqualTo_CFixedPoint( TntNum('tnt_picker'),
			### '(CFixedPoint)5' )]"`, its own `parentanchor = center` (legal: its
			### parent tnt_picker_overlay is a plain widget) and working defaults in
			### all four contract blocks, so nothing is overridden from here.
			###
			### ONE panel, no per-side twin, and its `visible` tests the INDEX ONLY:
			### the deal has exactly one betrothal, whose two halves are tnt_spouse_p
			### and tnt_spouse_r, so both marriage rows open the same editor and
			### there is nothing for tnt_picker_side to select.
			###
			### THIS INSTANTIATION WAS ONCE 90 LINES OF BLOCKOVERRIDES - two
			### candidate datamodels, a matrilineal toggle built from tnt_toggle_line
			### and a summary line - written from the naming contract alone, before
			### gui\tnt_panel_marriage.gui existed. Every one of them was deleted,
			### and it is worth recording WHY, because "the gui owner fills the
			### blocks" was a reasonable reading of the contract: three of the four
			### would have been WRONG. That file's line control is a patrilineal /
			### matrilineal button PAIR driven by tnt_marriage_set_patri and
			### tnt_marriage_set_matri, not a single toggle over tnt_marriage_matri;
			### its summary is a six-state ladder over tnt_marriage_legal and
			### tnt_marriage_betroth, not one sentence; and its rows carry an age
			### column the shipped tnt_picker_row_char does not have. Guessing four
			### block bodies across an agent boundary would have produced a panel
			### that loaded, looked plausible and drove the wrong effects.
			### THE RULE THIS LEAVES BEHIND: when a panel author ships working
			### defaults, the window instantiates and overrides nothing.
			############################################################
			### OUR OWN PAIR EDITOR IS SWITCHED OFF (V3).
			### Requested directly: "we do not need our intermediate window with its
			### custom picker and all its quirks, including its own list where the grand
			### wedding still cannot be turned off - clicking should open the vanilla
			### selection window straight away." The centre marriage line now calls
			### OpenPlayerInteraction, so nothing routes here any more; overlay index 5
			### is left reserved and the markup is kept for one release for easy revert.
			### tnt_panel_marriage.gui itself can be deleted in the cleanup pass.
			tnt_panel_marriage = {
				name = "tnt_panel_spouse"
				visible = no
			}

			############################################################
			### 6 / 7 / 10 - THE SIX MULTI-SELECT PANELS   (item 2.2)
			###
			### SIX LINES, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE INTEGRATION - the six ready-made
			### types in gui\tnt_panel_multiselect.gui each carry their own
			### `visible` (the frozen index 6 / 7 / 10 plus the side), their own
			### `parentanchor = center` and all four contract blocks already filled.
			### These six REPLACE the six single-object tnt_picker_panel instances
			### that stood at the same three indices in build 1; the deleted
			### variables tnt_title_p/_r, tnt_claim_p/_r, tnt_artifact_p/_r
			### (30-V2-DESIGN 3.1) are no longer named anywhere in this file.
			###
			### EVERY INSTANCE OVERRIDES `name`, and it is not cosmetic: each type
			### sets a name in its own body, and six same-named direct siblings of
			### this block make the engine log "Duplicate children with the same
			### name override previous widgets" - a line carrying tnt_, which the
			### acceptance bar forbids in error.log.
			###
			### These instantiations were also once ~50 lines each of hand-written
			### blockoverrides, and deleting them removed six wrong identifiers per
			### panel: the real setters are tnt_sel_<item>_<side>_add / _remove /
			### _clear, not the tnt_pick_<item>_<side>_set / _unset the design
			### sketch implied, and the panels also carry an empty-state key and,
			### on the two title panels, the domain pair - none of which this file
			### could have named. (They once wired a per-term cap flag too; see
			### the amended V3 note below for why that wiring is gone.)
			###
			### THE SIX ROW-LEVEL OPENERS CHANGED TOO, and this one is easy to get
			### wrong because the old name still exists and still works. The six
			### rows now call tnt_multi_<item>_<side>_open, NOT the shipped
			### tnt_pick_<item>_<side>_open. Both write the same tnt_picker /
			### tnt_picker_side pair, so both would make the panel appear - but only
			### the new one runs tnt_multi_prune_effect after the fill, which is what
			### removes the already-chosen objects from the available list. With the
			### old opener the panel would show every title in BOTH columns at once,
			### and since a row's column IS its selection state in the two-list
			### shape, that is not a cosmetic difference.
			############################################################
			### V3 ITEM - THE SELECTION CAP IS GONE, SO NOTHING MAY ANNOUNCE ONE.
			### AMENDED after the artifact-picker playtest bug ("Сверх предела их
			### домена" on the third artifact): this file used to override
			### block "tnt_multi_cap_visible" to `visible = no` on all seven
			### instances below, on the claim that "an instance-level blockoverride
			### is the last one in the chain, so it wins". THAT CLAIM WAS FALSE and
			### had no vanilla citation. A named block stays re-overridable only if
			### an override RE-DECLARES a named block inside itself (the ledger form
			### this mod itself documents in the header of type tnt_panel_multi,
			### gui\tnt_panel_multiselect.gui, citing GAME\gui\window_ledger.gui:
			### 3402-3407); the derived types'
			### plain `blockoverride "tnt_multi_cap_visible" { visible = ... }`
			### CONSUMED the slot, so the seven lines here matched nothing and the
			### stale cap flags (tnt_cap_hit_claim/artifact_*, still >= 3-triggered
			### in tnt_54_multiselect_values.txt) kept printing tnt_err_too_many.
			### FIXED AT THE SOURCE: the derived types no longer fill the block at
			### all (its type default is hidden), so the dead lines here were
			### deleted rather than kept as false comfort. If a cap ever comes
			### back, wire it in the DERIVED TYPES, not here.
			###
			### THE COUNT ITSELF STAYS AND IS UNTOUCHED: block "tnt_multi_counter"
			### keeps printing the panel's tnt_sel_count_<item>_<side> key, and the row
			### badges keep printing tnt_count_sel_*_value. Those loc strings once said
			### "of 3"; the loc author has long since reworded them to a bare count
			### ("Chosen: N") - it could not be done from a .gui, because a `text =`
			### cannot pass a parameter to a loc key.
			###
			### THERE IS NO CAP-DISABLED ADD BUTTON TO FIX. The panels never greyed
			### their rows: gui\tnt_panel_multiselect.gui's section 2 header says so
			### explicitly and no tnt_multi_row_* type carries an `enabled`, because
			### a per-row TntValid would be a scripted-gui evaluation per row per
			### frame (R9). The counter was the only channel, which is why it is the
			### only fix.
			tnt_panel_multi_title_p = {
				name = "tnt_panel_title_p"
			}

			tnt_panel_multi_title_r = {
				name = "tnt_panel_title_r"
			}

			####################################################################
			### RETIRED WITH THE GRANTED CLAIM - V13 USER ITEM 1. The two overlay
			### panels of the claim term, at index 7 side 0 and side 1. They must go
			### with the rows that opened them AND with the two types they
			### instantiate: `type tnt_panel_multi_claim_p` and
			### `type tnt_panel_multi_claim_r` are commented out in
			### gui\tnt_panel_multiselect.gui, and an instantiation of an undefined
			### type is an engine error - the atomic pair rule, in its .gui form.
			### A DESIGN REFUSAL, NOT A BUG FIX: vanilla gates the manufacture of
			### claims behind a LEARNING investment (task_fabricate_claim,
